\paragraph{Effect of sample count.}
Increasing $N$ from 2 to 16 expands oracle headroom fourfold ($+4.0$ to $+17.5$~pp) but yields no commensurate selection improvement, with the best signal achieving only $+0.27$~pp at $N{=}16$ (Table~\ref{tab:n_scaling_selection}).
Degeneracy drops monotonically (53\% to 11.5\%) without unlocking selection, consistent with the LoRA-rank ablation; at rank${=}8$ with $N{=}8$, degeneracy is 7.2\% and oracle headroom $+16.0$~pp, yet selection is \textit{worse} ($-0.47$~pp).

