VC selection degrades with increasing $N$ ($-2.27$~pp at $N{=}2$ to $-4.18$~pp at $N{=}32$), consistent with mode-seeking bias in voting-based selection as the candidate pool grows.
Bootstrap significance testing at $N{=}32$ ($B{=}10{,}000$) confirms that LP shows a consistent positive trend ($+0.95$~pp, $p{=}0.091$) but does not reach significance at $\alpha{=}0.05$, while all signals except VC significantly outperform random selection ($p{<}0.001$; Table~\ref{tab:bootstrap_n32})---the gap is not a statistical artifact but a structural limitation.

